IMPORT prelude

-- National University of Singapore (Corporatisation) Act 2005 (Singapore) -- what the Minister must consent to and what happens
-- without consent (s 7), how public money may be spent (s 8), the duty to give information and its offence (s 9), student bodies
-- (ss 10, 19), transferred staff and pending discipline (ss 13, 14, 16, 17), what happens to the Academic Staff Provident Fund money
-- of a member when the Fund was dissolved (s 18, First Schedule paras 1(2), 5, 6, 11, 13, 15, 23, 24, 33-41, 46, 48), and the Register
-- of Graduates (s 20, Second Schedule).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/NUSCA2005.txt. The deposit says it "incorporates
-- all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021"; the latest amendment annotated
-- in the body is [40/2018] (s 7(2)), and the First Schedule carries [S 633/2007]. SSO marked it "Current version as at 03 Oct 2026".
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0194 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked
-- a sharper question yet. SCOPED to the provisions a person meets: a supplier or anyone asked for records, a student, a graduate,
-- a member of staff, and a former ASPF member.
-- Not encoded: the company's function and the Minister's frameworks and directions (ss 3-5), trustee appointment beyond s 7(1)(e)
-- (s 6), the vesting of property and its land-registration machinery (s 12(1)-(9)), the continuation of contracts and proceedings
-- (ss 12(10), (11), 15) beyond a mention, the ASPF notice and its deemed service (First Schedule paras 2-4), the accounts and audit
-- (paras 11(2), 12), the mortgage transfers (paras 25-29), the disclosure rules (paras 30, 31) and the evidence rule (para 49).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `National University of Singapore (Corporatisation) Act 2005`

§§ `7 -- what needs the Minister's prior written consent`

-- s 7(1): "The prior written consent of the Minister is required for -- (a) the admission of any person as a member of the
-- university company and the removal of any such member; (b) the disposal of the whole or substantially the whole of the
-- university company's undertaking or property; (c) the voluntary winding up of the university company; (d) the addition, deletion
-- or alteration of any provision of the constituent documents ...; and (e) the removal of any trustee from the Board."
-- (2): these apply "in addition to" the Companies Act 1967 and the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018.
-- (3): "Any act done or agreement made in contravention of subsection (1) has no effect and is unenforceable at law."
-- s 6: the Board consists of such trustees "as the Minister may appoint"; appointing a trustee is not in the s 7 list.
DECLARE CompanyAct IS ONE OF
    `admitting a member of the company`
    `removing a member of the company`
    `selling substantially the whole undertaking`
    `selling one building`
    `voluntarily winding up the company`
    `amending the articles of association`
    `removing a trustee`
    `appointing a trustee`
    `conferring an honorary degree`

GIVEN `the company act` IS A CompanyAct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister's prior written consent is required` IF
    CONSIDER `the company act`
    WHEN `selling one building` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `appointing a trustee` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `conferring an honorary degree` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- "Prior" and "written" are both conditions. The Act says nothing of ratification after the event; this encoding reads s 7(3) as
-- leaving a later consent without effect on an act already done (an inference from "prior").
GIVEN `the company act` IS A CompanyAct, `consent was in writing` IS A BOOLEAN, `consent came before the act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the act has no effect and is unenforceable` IF
    `the Minister's prior written consent is required` `the company act`
    AND NOT (`consent was in writing` AND `consent came before the act`)

§§ `8 -- money from Parliament`

-- s 8(1): the Minister "must pay" such moneys "as Parliament may provide". (2): those moneys "may only be applied or expended by the
-- university company for such objects provided by its constituent documents as the Minister may allow". Money from other sources
-- (fees, gifts) is outside s 8(2); the encoding returns TRUE for it, which is a statement about s 8 only.
GIVEN `paid under s 8(1)` IS A BOOLEAN, `an object in the constituent documents` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Minister allows the object` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 8 permits the spending` IF
    IF `paid under s 8(1)` THEN `an object in the constituent documents` AND `the Minister allows the object` ELSE TRUE

§§ `9 -- access to records and the information offence`

-- s 9(2): the Minister or an authorised person "may require ANY person to provide him or her with any information in that person's
-- possession, or to which that person has access", considered necessary for ascertaining whether s 8 moneys were properly applied
-- and "any other matters". (4): "Any person who, without reasonable excuse, fails to comply with any requirement ... under
-- subsection (2) or who otherwise hinders, obstructs or delays the Minister or an authorised person ... shall be guilty of an
-- offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $1,000." No imprisonment is provided.
-- Read literally, "without reasonable excuse" governs the failure to comply; the hindering limb has its own "who" and no excuse.
-- That is this encoding's reading, not a decided point.
GIVEN `failed to comply with a requirement` IS A BOOLEAN, `had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN, `hindered, obstructed or delayed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a s 9(4) offence is committed` IF
        (`failed to comply with a requirement` AND (NOT `had a reasonable excuse`))
    OR  `hindered, obstructed or delayed`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine under s 9(4)` MEANS 1000

§§ `10, 19 -- student bodies`

-- s 10(1): "Despite anything to the contrary in the Societies Act 1966, the provisions of that Act have effect in relation to any
-- student body constituted pursuant to the provisions of the constituent documents". (2): the Minister for societies may by order
-- in the Gazette exempt such a body "from all or any of the provisions". s 19: on 1 April 2006 the NUS Students' Union and its
-- constituent bodies "are deemed to be constituted pursuant to" the constituent documents.
-- The encoding returns whether the Societies Act applies at all; a partial exemption leaves it applying.
GIVEN `constituted under the constituent documents` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Students' Union or a constituent body` IS A BOOLEAN, `wholly exempted by Gazette order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Societies Act applies to the student body` IF
    (NOT `wholly exempted by Gazette order`)
    AND (`constituted under the constituent documents` OR `the Students' Union or a constituent body`)

§§ `13, 14, 16, 17 -- staff and pending discipline`

-- s 13(1): from 1 April 2006 all persons employed immediately before that date by the predecessor university "are transferred to
-- the service of the university company on terms no less favourable". (2): "Until the terms and conditions of service are drawn up
-- by the university company, the scheme and terms and conditions of service in the predecessor university continue to apply".
GIVEN `employed by the predecessor immediately before 1 April 2006` IS A BOOLEAN, `the company has drawn up its terms` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the predecessor's terms still govern` IF
    `employed by the predecessor immediately before 1 April 2006` AND NOT `the company has drawn up its terms`

-- s 14(2): in any term relating to length of service the company must "provide for the recognition of service under the predecessor
-- university by that person to be service under the university company".
GIVEN `years with the predecessor` IS A NUMBER, `years with the company` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`recognised length of service` MEANS `years with the predecessor` PLUS `years with the company`

-- s 16(1): disciplinary proceedings commenced before 1 April 2006 against a transferred employee or "any student of the predecessor
-- university" and pending on that date "must ... be carried on and completed by the university company".
GIVEN `against a transferred employee or a student` IS A BOOLEAN, `commenced before 1 April 2006` IS A BOOLEAN, `pending on 1 April 2006` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the company must complete the proceedings` IF
    `against a transferred employee or a student` AND `commenced before 1 April 2006` AND `pending on 1 April 2006`

-- s 17: the company "may reprimand, reduce in rank, retire, dismiss or punish" a person for misconduct or neglect while employed by
-- the predecessor "which would have rendered the person liable" had the person stayed there and "if this Act had not been enacted".
GIVEN `misconduct while with the predecessor` IS A BOOLEAN, `would have been punishable there` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the company may punish pre-transfer misconduct` IF
    `misconduct while with the predecessor` AND `would have been punishable there`

§§ `18 and First Schedule -- the end of the Academic Staff Provident Fund`

-- para 1(2): a relevant person "is treated as uncontactable if -- (a) the person does not have a CPF account; and (b) the university
-- company is not in possession of any of the following details or documents ... which are necessary for the opening of a CPF
-- account: (i) the person's nationality; (ii) ... national registration identification number; (iii) [for a non-citizen] passport
-- number and foreign identification number ...; (iv) the person's date of birth, despite reasonable efforts made by the university
-- company to obtain those details or documents."
--
-- "not in possession of any of" reads literally as holding NONE of them. Read for purpose (the details are "necessary for the
-- opening of a CPF account"), lacking ANY ONE would do. Both readings are encoded; they part company when some details are held.
-- Identification is one flag here, standing for (ii) or (iii) as the person's citizenship requires.
GIVEN `has a CPF account` IS A BOOLEAN, `nationality held` IS A BOOLEAN, `identification held` IS A BOOLEAN, `date of birth held` IS A BOOLEAN, `reasonable efforts made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `uncontactable, literal reading` IF
    (NOT `has a CPF account`) AND (NOT `nationality held`) AND (NOT `identification held`) AND (NOT `date of birth held`) AND `reasonable efforts made`

GIVEN `has a CPF account` IS A BOOLEAN, `nationality held` IS A BOOLEAN, `identification held` IS A BOOLEAN, `date of birth held` IS A BOOLEAN, `reasonable efforts made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `uncontactable, purposive reading` IF
    (NOT `has a CPF account`) AND `reasonable efforts made`
    AND ((NOT `nationality held`) OR (NOT `identification held`) OR (NOT `date of birth held`))

-- Where the money went on 28 December 2007 (s 18(3): "The university company must, on 28 December 2007, dissolve the ASPF Scheme").
-- para 40-41: an uncontactable person's moneys "must not be transferred to the CPF Board" but go to an account "in the name of the
-- university company as trustee". para 1(1): a "deceased relevant person" is one "who is not uncontactable and who dies before
-- 28 December 2007"; paras 33, 34, 39(1): those moneys go to a trustee account and are then paid "to the trustees or legal personal
-- representatives". para 5: a person "55 years of age or above as at 28 December 2007" may choose (a) transfer to CPF or (b) payment
-- to him or her "subject to the condition that he or she -- (i) has sufficient money set aside for the purposes of section 15(6) of the
-- Central Provident Fund Act 1953; or (ii) sets aside an amount". para 6: if the company "is not notified of the option selected ...
-- in the manner and by the date specified", the moneys "must be transferred to the CPF Board". para 13(b): everyone else's moneys
-- go to the CPF Board.
-- That an opt-out who fails the para 5(b) condition falls back to CPF is an inference; the Schedule does not say.
DECLARE AspfOutcome IS ONE OF
    `transferred to the CPF Board`
    `paid out to the member`
    `held by the company as trustee for the estate`
    `held by the company as trustee until claimed`

GIVEN `uncontactable` IS A BOOLEAN, `died before 28 December 2007` IS A BOOLEAN, `age on 28 December 2007` IS A NUMBER, `chose payment out` IS A BOOLEAN, `notified the choice in time` IS A BOOLEAN, `CPF set-aside met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN AspfOutcome
`where the ASPF moneys went` MEANS
    IF `uncontactable` THEN `held by the company as trustee until claimed`
    ELSE IF `died before 28 December 2007` THEN `held by the company as trustee for the estate`
         ELSE IF `age on 28 December 2007` AT LEAST 55 AND `chose payment out` AND `notified the choice in time` AND `CPF set-aside met`
              THEN `paid out to the member`
              ELSE `transferred to the CPF Board`

-- para 15: "Every living relevant person who is not uncontactable and is not already a CPF member immediately before 28 December
-- 2007 is deemed to be a CPF member on that date". para 16: bound by the CPF Act and entitled to its rights.
GIVEN `living on 28 December 2007` IS A BOOLEAN, `uncontactable` IS A BOOLEAN, `already a CPF member` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `deemed a CPF member` IF
    `living on 28 December 2007` AND (NOT `uncontactable`) AND NOT `already a CPF member`

-- para 11(1)(b): the company must "compute the respective share of the balance of the assets of the ASPF (if any) in respect of each
-- relevant person ... pro rata to the average of the balances of ASPF moneys in his or her account at the end of each quarter";
-- para 20: transferred 30 days after 28 December 2007 and credited "to the ordinary account". (30 days after 28 December 2007 is
-- 27 January 2008, the date paras 35 and 42 name; counted by hand, not by the encoding.)
GIVEN `the balance of the assets` IS A NUMBER, `the person's average quarter-end balance` IS A NUMBER, `the total of all averages` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the person's share of the surplus` MEANS
    `the balance of the assets` TIMES `the person's average quarter-end balance` DIVIDED BY `the total of all averages`

-- para 7: "All premiums paid towards any Part V Assurance, whether using ASPF moneys or cash, before 28 December 2007, are deemed to
-- have been paid with ASPF moneys." para 23: a living relevant person who "used ASPF moneys for paying the premium" may afterwards
-- pay it from the CPF ordinary account. para 24: one who "did not ... use his or her ASPF moneys" may not.
-- Does para 7's deeming make a cash payer someone who "used ASPF moneys"? Paras 23-24 speak of actual use and para 24 is "to avoid
-- doubt"; para 7 deems every premium ASPF-paid. Both readings are encoded.
GIVEN `paid a premium with ASPF moneys` IS A BOOLEAN, `paid a premium in cash` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may pay the premium from CPF, actual-use reading` IF
    `paid a premium with ASPF moneys`

GIVEN `paid a premium with ASPF moneys` IS A BOOLEAN, `paid a premium in cash` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may pay the premium from CPF, para 7 deeming reading` IF
    `paid a premium with ASPF moneys` OR `paid a premium in cash`

-- para 46: anyone entitled to money held for an uncontactable person "may apply to the university company to claim" it. para 48:
-- once a CPF account is opened, "(a) where the relevant person is below 55 years of age, transfer ... to that CPF account; or (b)
-- where the relevant person is 55 years of age or above, give the relevant person an option". Age here is not fixed at
-- 28 December 2007 as in para 5; the encoding takes the age when the account is opened (an inference from the present tense).
GIVEN `age when the CPF account is opened` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the late claimant has a choice` IF
    `age when the CPF account is opened` AT LEAST 55

§§ `20 and Second Schedule -- the Register of Graduates`

-- Second Schedule para 1: the company "must maintain a Register of Graduates" of (a) members of the Guild of Graduates of the
-- University of Singapore immediately before 8 August 1980 and all persons on whom its degrees had been conferred; (b) members of the
-- predecessor university's Guild immediately before 1 April 2006 and its degree holders; (c) "all graduates of the University".
-- para 2: Parts A, B and C respectively. para 3: anyone on the Register "may receive such documents or other papers of the
-- University as determined by the Board".
DECLARE Graduate IS ONE OF
    `a University of Singapore graduate`
    `a graduate of the old statutory NUS`
    `a graduate of the corporatised NUS`
    `a graduate of another university`

DECLARE RegisterPart IS ONE OF
    `Part A`
    `Part B`
    `Part C`
    `not on the Register`

GIVEN `the graduate` IS A Graduate
GIVETH A RegisterPart
`the Part of the Register` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the graduate`
    WHEN `a University of Singapore graduate` THEN `Part A`
    WHEN `a graduate of the old statutory NUS` THEN `Part B`
    WHEN `a graduate of the corporatised NUS` THEN `Part C`
    OTHERWISE `not on the Register`
